      "artist": "Government of Brunei",
      "description": "His Excellency the high commissioner of Brunei, Sir Anthony Abell, arrived in Brunei from Kuching on 13 November 1956 for an official visit and departed for Kuching on 19 November. This photograph shows Sir Anthony Abell inspecting the Honour Guard of the Brunei Town Police on the morning of 14 November before visiting the British Resident’s Office. Beside Sir Anthony Abell are the chief police officer of Brunei, Mr. A.N. Outram, and the officer in charge of the Brunei Police District, ASP Pengiran Jaya bin Pengiran Haji Rajid. During his visit, His Excellency held consultations with His Majesty the Sultan and senior government officials, inspected key construction projects under the national development plans, visited Tutong to observe road construction progress, and accompanied His Majesty on a visit to Temburong.",
